      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:5:3:158:2",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ( صلى الله عليه وآله ) أَيُّ امْرَأَةٍ تَطَيَّبَتْ ثُمَّ خَرَجَتْ مِنْ بَيْتِهَا فَهِيَ تُلْعَنُ حَتَّى تَرْجِعَ إِلَى بَيْتِهَا مَتَى مَا رَجَعَتْ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ibn Abu Umeyr, form Ibrahim Bin Abdul Hameed, from Al Waleed Bin Sabeeh, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Rasool-Allah<sup>saww</sup> said: ‘Whichever woman perfumes herself, then goes out from her house, so she is cursed until she return to her house whenever she returns’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Ibn abu ‘Umayr has narrated from Ibrahim ibn ‘Abd al-Hamid from al-Walid ibn Sabih who has said the following: “Abu ’Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said that the Messenger of Allah, O Allah, grant compensation to Muhammad and his family worthy of their services to Your cause, has said, ‘If a woman wears perfumes then goes out of her house, she is then cursed and condemned until she returns to her home whenever she does.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
